{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/id","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV2idSSSgvp","symbolKind":"property","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"title":"id","roleHeading":"Instance Property"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate"]]},"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specifies an id reference.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"let","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"id","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Discussion","anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Maps to the MusicXML "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":" attribute."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/id"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"title":"MXLArpeggiate","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","abstract":[{"text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate/id":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate\/id","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"id"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS"},{"kind":"text","text":"?"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate\/id","abstract":[{"text":"The optional-unique-id attribute group allows an element to optionally specify an ID that is unique to the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"entire document. This attribute group is not used for a required id attribute, or for an id attribute that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"specifies an id reference.","type":"text"}],"title":"id"}}}